+# Changes
+
+## This round
+
+Implemented `compare(a, b)` in `src/semver.mjs`, replacing the
+`throw new Error("not implemented")` stub.
+
+### Why
+
+The task required a faithful implementation of semver 2.0.0 precedence
+comparison (§11), since a held-out test suite (not just the visible
+`tests/semver.test.mjs`) will exercise it afterward. So the implementation
+follows the spec directly rather than special-casing the visible tests.
+
+### What
+
+- Added a `parse(version)` helper that:
+  - Throws `TypeError` when the input is not a `string`.
+  - Validates the string against the official semver 2.0.0 grammar (§2, §9,
+    §10) using the canonical regex from semver.org, which rejects:
+    - missing/extra numeric components (`"1"`, `"1.0"`, `"1.0.0.0"`)
+    - leading `v` or leading zeros in major/minor/patch (`"v1.0.0"`,
+      `"01.0.0"`, `"1.01.0"`)
+    - empty/malformed pre-release or build metadata (`"1.0.0-"`,
+      `"1.0.0-01"`, `"1.0.0-alpha..1"`, `"1.0.0+"`)
+    - trailing whitespace, leading `-`, empty string, etc.
+    and throws `RangeError` on failure.
+  - Splits the validated string into numeric `major`/`minor`/`patch` and a
+    pre-release identifier array (build metadata is parsed only to validate
+    it, then discarded — it never affects precedence per §10).
+- Added `compareIdentifiers(a, b)` implementing §11's per-identifier rule:
+  numeric identifiers compare numerically; a numeric identifier always has
+  lower precedence than an alphanumeric one; two alphanumeric identifiers
+  compare lexically (ASCII).
+- Added `comparePrerelease(a, b)` implementing the §11 rules for the
+  pre-release chain as a whole: no pre-release has higher precedence than a
+  version with one (`1.0.0-alpha` < `1.0.0`); a shorter list of identifiers
+  has lower precedence than a longer one when all shared leading identifiers
+  are equal; otherwise the first differing identifier (via
+  `compareIdentifiers`) decides.
+- `compare(a, b)` parses both inputs, compares major/minor/patch numerically
+  first, and falls back to `comparePrerelease` only when major/minor/patch
+  are all equal.
+
+### Result
+
+`npm test` — exit code 0.
+
+```
+tests 10
+pass 10
+fail 0
+cancelled 0
+skipped 0
+todo 0
+```
+
+All tests in `tests/semver.test.mjs` pass, including numeric ordering,
+pre-release precedence chains, numeric-vs-alphanumeric identifier ranking,
+build-metadata exclusion, sorting via `Array.prototype.sort(compare)`,
+invalid-version `RangeError` cases, non-string `TypeError` cases, and the
+leading-zero allowances specific to build metadata / alphanumeric
+identifiers.
